{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle","id":379384,"title":"Centimani based chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-23T12:42:54-08:00","id":379384,"title":"Centimani based chronicle","content":"Excuse me if this is a bit of a ramble.<br /> I am very new to PtC. With the other games I just <i>get</i> it and just love them. This game seems to have the wrong protagonists. In this game it seems to me as if the centimani have certain parts that should belong to the normal protagonists. How can a group build good relationships with another group, by saying all my own values are wrong and all the other group's values is the gold standard?<br /> <br /> I may have it totally wrong here though, because the word &quot;created&quot; could imply that the promethean was created differently then he himself would have done, had he been mature enough to know what it is that he himself wants. The way PtC is written now I am feeling as if the promethean can't succeed because he needs to become something else other then who he is, a thought that will destroy any self-esteem. <br /> <br /> Having said that, I do see the need for Prometheans to become something that can have good rewarding relationships with humans, despite not being human. I am thinking optimal relationships with humans without sacrificing one's identity.<br /> Has anyone here ever ran a Centimani-based chronicle? How did it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","name":"Thinking_Point","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T13:06:01-08:00","id":379434,"title":"","content":"I've never run a Centimani-based chronicle, so I can't quite speak to that, but I'm actually have a little trouble parsing your concerns about the setting and your feeling that the Centimani should be the protagonists. Why do you feel that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T14:36:06-08:00","id":379516,"title":"","content":"Worded a different way: Is there any connection between the Torment that a Promethean feels and being able to accept who one is right now. I think of acceptance as the opposite of Torment. Is it is possible to change without accepting and acknowledging what one is now? The Centimani start with accepting themselves. I would think that after they have come to peace with what they really are, it would be easier them to deal with the quality of relationships with humans. With the Centimani what I don't like is how they decide to react with humans. I really have difficulty thinking of how Prometheans can change to human, but if it is possible, it must start with accepting what they are right now. One after thought is that the practice of Cuprum would seem to be one way to attain that acceptance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","user":"Thinking_Point","date":". 01-23-2015, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","name":"Thinking_Point","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T18:37:47-08:00","id":379723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thinking_Point</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle#post379384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me if this is a bit of a ramble.<br /> I am very new to PtC. With the other games I just <i>get</i> it and just love them. This game seems to have the wrong protagonists. In this game it seems to me as if the centimani have certain parts that should belong to the normal protagonists. How can a group build good relationships with another group, by saying all my own values are wrong and all the other group's values is the gold standard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy, this again.<br /> <br /> The Created do not <i>have </i>their own values. They have a base nature dictated by their animating humour, leftover impulses from when their body was host to a human being, inclinations imparted to them by their Azoth, and whatever personality they develop over top of all that.<br /> <br /> The Created are not aiming to &quot;build good relationships with another group.&quot; They are aiming to <i>make it so that the raw essence of mutability that rolls off them in waves</i><i> stops <b>leaking into the world and ruining everything with its undirected erosion of all things.</b></i> Torment isn't societal pressure, it's the Promethean's base state asserting itself over their better nature and their ability to act like a being that isn't defined by what it is.<br /> <br /> When the Created say they're trying to become human, they mean they're trying to become something that can compromise, innovate, imagine, hope, and exist without inherent reason. Virtually every monster in the World of Darkness that didn't used to be human or become more human is incapable of those things by nature.<br /> <br /> The Centimani are aligning themselves with a force that <i>mutates their bodies and disintegrates their minds</i> as part of their having given up on any hope of becoming something other than a monster. That's not self-acceptance, that's despairing of any chance at self-improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T03:19:09-08:00","id":379930,"title":"","content":"<b>Thinking_Point</b>, you are looking here for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transhumanism\" target=\"_blank\">transhuman</a> perspective on <b>Promethean</b> - and it was loudly asserted by devs &quot;small minority&quot; of players on forum. As quick rule I just say you do not need to become Centimani to have goal other than become human as Created - you can play Argentum, Ferrum and Plumbum for this. You just need to remember that you will not end your Pilgrimage, as it <b>is</b> you goal now. Longer answer you will find in out enclave on this subforum, topic <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here\">Promethean and Transhumanism Goes Here</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-24-2015, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T13:02:54-08:00","id":380402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=379930#post379930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking_Point, you are looking here for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transhumanism\" target=\"_blank\">transhuman</a> perspective on Promethean - <b>and it was loudly asserted by devs &quot;small minority&quot; of players on forum.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to stop lying, man.<br /> <br /> None of the devs have the free time to be anything approaching &quot;loud&quot; about any given aspect of the game and the extent to which they've commented on the subject of quote-unquote-transhumanism it's been to the effect of &quot;we're not writing the games to support humans becoming monsters as a generally positive change,&quot; not any of this nonsense about claiming one party or another is a vocal minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-24-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T01:22:15-08:00","id":380854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thinking_Point</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=379516#post379516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Centimani start with accepting themselves. I would think that after they have come to peace with what they really are, it would be easier them to deal with the quality of relationships with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you say they accept themselves, the Centimani are accepting themselves <i>as monsters</i>. Moreover, the Centimani roll around in the muck of their monstrousness, caking it onto their skin so they can wear their scarred self-image on their flesh. It's like ascribing yourself the label of &quot;hideous, unlovable freak&quot; -- it's not a healthy attitude.<br /> <br /> If a character is exploring their &quot;Promethean-ness&quot;, or is asking what exactly a Promethean is (other than human, of course), they're definitely on Plumbum and not Centimanus. It's in the Magnum Opus book, so if you've only read the PtC core that's why you haven't heard of it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/first-principles-basic-refinements/\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a blog post that has some more intel on what Plumbum's going to look like in second edition.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T07:02:43-08:00","id":380956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=379930#post379930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thinking_Point</b>, you are looking here for <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transhumanism\" target=\"_blank\">transhuman</a> perspective on <b>Promethean</b> - and it was loudly asserted by devs &quot;small minority&quot; of players on forum.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Promethean</b> is not written to be a transhumanist game. Is that...hard to understand? There are games like that out there, and hell, if <i>you</i> want to play <b>Promethean</b> like that, I'm not going to tell you you're playing it wrong. But that's not what we're writing. <br /> <br /> I mean, like, you don't show up at a Billy Joel concert and start complaining that he's not playing hair metal. Hair metal is awesome (I grew up in the 80s!), but it is it's own thing. Other things don't need to be that thing, just because they're expressed in the same medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T08:39:16-08:00","id":381031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=379723#post379723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh boy, this again.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Grass,_Running_Water\" target=\"_blank\">Hey, where'd all this water come from?</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T12:40:56-08:00","id":381263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=380956#post380956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Promethean</b> is not written to be a transhumanist game. Is that...hard to understand? There are games like that out there, and hell, if <i>you</i> want to play <b>Promethean</b> like that, I'm not going to tell you you're playing it wrong. But that's not what we're writing.<br /> <br /> I mean, like, you don't show up at a Billy Joel concert and start complaining that he's not playing hair metal. Hair metal is awesome (I grew up in the 80s!), but it is it's own thing. Other things don't need to be that thing, just because they're expressed in the same medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue that people think is that since Prometheans are already on the path (Pilgrimage) to humanity, they can stop and look for other paths that lead to other places besides humanity.<br /> <br /> However, the game does not support that as there are other WoD lines that already cover those themes (Again, Mage comes to mind with leaving humanity behind for Godhood). <br /> <br /> A Promethean can step off the path to humanity but in doing so, the first lines of a epic poem come to mind.<br /> <br /> Midway upon the journey of our life<br /> I found myself within a forest dark,<br /> For the straightforward pathway had been lost.<br /> Ah me! how hard a thing it is to say<br /> What was this forest savage, rough, and stern,<br /> Which in the very thought renews the fear.<br /> So bitter is it, death is little more;<br /> But of the good to treat, which there I found,<br /> Speak will I of the other things I saw there.<br /> I cannot well repeat how there I entered,<br /> So full was I of slumber at the moment<br /> In which I had abandoned the true way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T13:56:20-08:00","id":381327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=381263#post381263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Promethean can step off the path to humanity but in doing so, the first lines of a epic poem come to mind.<br /> <br /> Midway upon the journey of our life<br /> I found myself within a forest dark,<br /> For the straightforward pathway had been lost.<br /> Ah me! how hard a thing it is to say<br /> What was this forest savage, rough, and stern,<br /> Which in the very thought renews the fear.<br /> So bitter is it, death is little more;<br /> But of the good to treat, which there I found,<br /> Speak will I of the other things I saw there.<br /> I cannot well repeat how there I entered,<br /> So full was I of slumber at the moment<br /> In which I had abandoned the true way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I may elaborate a bit on this, Dante's Divine Comedy is, at least under one of its <i>many </i>layers of reading, a voyage that allows its main character to purify and save its soul. A Pilgrimage, if you will.<br /> <br /> I won't deny that the idea of a chronicle in which a Promethean Dante (a Ulgan, because of course), after a confrontation with some Pandorans while on the run ponders about its existence but thanks to the intervention of a powerful Quashmallim embarks on a journey through the depths of the hidden worlds of the NWoD with the help of an entity (Ancient ghost? Spirit? Vampire?) who introduces itself as a poet from Imperial Rome in order to discover the nature of the Soul and complete its pilgrimage is an intriguing, if impractical, one.<br /> <br /> Ok, thread derail over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-26-2015, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T15:41:01-08:00","id":381401,"title":"","content":"And here I thought my idea of re-imagining the Inferno into a Sci-Fi space exploration story was nifty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T11:19:11-08:00","id":383368,"title":"","content":"A Promethean is a half-formed creature animated with the volatile energy of transformation and decay. This energy is ultimately chaotic and will eventually tear them apart, eroding their mind and body, unless it is harnessed to transform them into something more stable. It isn't a matter of learning to love themselves. They are on fire and need to put the fire out before it consumes them. Until they do, it will eventually set everything around them on fire, too. Becoming a Centimanus is ultimately self-destructive, not self-accepting. For whatever reason, you've given up trying to become whole and stable. You may want to flail around, using the fire to destroy as much as possible until you burn out. You may be exhausted by the effort of finishing your creation and just want to sit in solitude and burn to ash. You may think that you can harness the fire... but you're wrong. It will destroy you.<br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}